(EXP-97, folded into EXP-83: a radix cast reads the whole text as digits
 of its base, and any other character makes the text not a number in that
 base (LANGUAGE.md:2158-2165), so each cast below raises the error flag
 and its declaration holds 0 (LANGUAGE.md:2243-2248). Up to vox 0.4.15 a
 radix cast stopped at the first invalid character instead, and this
 probe printed 18 for "12g5" as a hex number with the flag clear
 (Discrepancy 2, resolved by vox #281). Re-recorded 2026-10-13 on vox main
 a0a2ecc.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox EXP-97.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   hex partial set the flag
   0
   base 5 fully invalid set the flag
   0
   hex fully invalid set the flag
   0
)
a text called mixed is "12g5".
a number called 'from mixed' is mixed as a hex number.
On error Print "hex partial set the flag".
Print 'from mixed'.
a text called impossible is "abc".
a number called 'from impossible' is impossible as a base5 number.
On error Print "base 5 fully invalid set the flag".
Print 'from impossible'.
a text called letters is "zzz".
a number called 'from letters' is letters as a hex number.
On error Print "hex fully invalid set the flag".
Print 'from letters'.
